From f6ff266d7b9ee5abbda9ef495bfee7a308e7d57d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 20:45:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0037 a restart cannot open a second hedge (5590 passed)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

INVENTORY D3: CarryEngine.position lived in memory. A container that died
holding a hedge came back FLAT, CarryRisk.has_open_pair read the empty engine,
and the book opened a SECOND hedge against the same margin and the same
liquidation price. reconcile_pair existed with zero call sites; the
directional orphan check only runs for a linear-category client and the carry
client is spot. Drill step 5 could not pass.

Two halves, neither optional.

THE LEDGER. persistence gains one row (`carry_position`): the whole engine
state as JSON, written on EVERY state change — open, rebalance, unwind,
emergency unwind, halt. The engine takes `persist` as a REQUIRED argument; a
write that fails HALTS the book (LEDGER_WRITE_FAILED), because a book whose
ledger is behind its orders is exactly the state this patch exists to prevent.
`load_carry_position()` returns None only when no carry book ever ran: a flat
book writes a row saying flat, and that difference is what separates "nothing
to resume" from "the ledger was lost".

THE VENUE. CarryBroker.get_perp_position and get_open_carry_orders, both
raising rather than reporting zero. Open-order policy: EVERY open order on the
perp symbol counts (that instrument is the book's), but on spot only orders
this book placed — an overlay client's own spot orders are their business, and
halting the hedge because they placed one would be the book seizing their
wallet.

THE COMPARISON. plan_cold_start() is pure and has its own tests: CLEAN,
RESUME, or HALT. It halts on a venue position the ledger never saw, a ledger
pair the venue does not have, a size mismatch beyond dust, an overlay whose
inventory has left, an execution mode that changed between runs, a ledger that
was already HALTED, and any open order. It NEVER edits the ledger — the
disagreement is the evidence a human needs. TradingBot.carry_cold_start runs
it in startup() BEFORE engine.reconcile, trips the kill switch on HALT and
refuses to start; an unreadable ledger or venue is also a refusal, never an
assumption of flat.

Also 0037 (D16): session_tail told the truth about itself. Run outside the
virtualenv it printed `GATE STILL FALSE?: NO (UNREADABLE: No module named
numpy)` — which reads as "the gate opened". It now has three outcomes and
three exit codes: 0 holds, 1 MOVED, 2 could not be read, plus the line telling
you which interpreter to use. A tool that cannot tell False from cannot-tell
would hide a real violation behind the same word.

Tests first: bot/tests/test_carry_cold_start.py, 30 new; 5 more in
test_session_tail.py. No existing assertion changed; stub stores gained the
two ledger methods and engines gained `persist`, both of which production
requires.

Files: bot/carry_engine.py carry_broker.py persistence.py main.py,
bot/tools/session_tail.py, bot/docs/human/INVENTORY.md, 9 test files.

